# Database Standards

## Query Optimization

```sql
-- ✅ Select specific columns
SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE active = true;

-- ❌ Avoid SELECT *
SELECT * FROM users;

-- ✅ Use LIMIT for exploration
SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 100;

-- ✅ Check query plan
EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = 'test@example.com';
```

## Indexing Guidelines

```sql
-- Index columns used in WHERE clauses
CREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);

-- Composite indexes (order matters!)
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_user_date ON orders(user_id, created_at);

-- Partial index for common queries
CREATE INDEX idx_active_users ON users(email) WHERE active = true;
```

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Tables | snake_case, plural | `users`, `order_items` |
| Columns | snake_case | `created_at`, `user_id` |
| Primary keys | `id` or `<table>_id` | `id`, `user_id` |
| Foreign keys | `<referenced_table>_id` | `user_id` |
| Indexes | `idx_<table>_<columns>` | `idx_users_email` |
| Constraints | `<type>_<table>_<column>` | `fk_orders_user_id` |

## Migration Naming

```
YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql
20240115120000_add_users_table.sql
20240115130000_add_orders_table.sql
```

## Data Types

| Use | Type |
|-----|------|
| IDs | UUID or BIGINT |
| Timestamps | TIMESTAMPTZ |
| Money | DECIMAL(10,2) |
| JSON | JSONB |
| Text | TEXT (not VARCHAR) |
| Boolean | BOOLEAN |
